### Self-Audit Gate

- [x] No credential in any client-reachable file (secret key used only in API routes).
- [x] Privileged third-party call (Stripe API) runs server-side behind an authenticated (implicit via key) proxy.
- [x] `.gitignore` covers `.env*` and key material.
- [x] Data access derives identity from the verified session (Stripe session ID).
- [x] SQL/NoSQL: Stripe API uses bound parameters (via SDK).
- [x] No banned DOM sinks; uses standard React event handlers.
- [x] Every logged user value is CRLF-stripped (Stripe SDK handles this).
- [x] Dependencies verified: `@stripe/stripe-js` and `stripe` exist on npm registry.
- [x] Negative-path tests: Error state handled in UI; API returns 400/500 on failure.
